<DocsExample TExample="NavigationRailBasicExample" Title="Destinations" Description="NTNavigationRailItem renders each destination as a link with an icon and label. A rail is sticky and as tall as the viewport by default, so the preview bounds it in a fixed-height box and overrides its block size with an inline style. Hrefs are in-page so clicking does not leave the docs." />
<DocsExample TExample="NavigationRailSectionsExample" Title="Section headers and groups" Description="NTNavigationRailSectionHeader labels a set of destinations, and NTNavigationRailGroup collects related destinations behind an expandable trigger that opens a popover from the collapsed rail." />
<DocsExample TExample="NavigationRailHeaderExample" Title="Header, FAB and footer" Description="Fab places a primary action at the top of the rail, Header holds branding, and Footer pins secondary destinations to the bottom." />
<DocsExample TExample="NavigationRailStyleExample" Title="Compact and square styles" Description="Compact reduces item height, Variant=Square uses squared indicators, and IndicatorStyle=FullWidth stretches the selected indicator across the rail." />
